{"id":"mekong-bike","title":"The Mekong by bike: Vientiane to Phnom Penh","who":"Classic route · Laos and Cambodia along the river","when":"November to February (dry and cooler)","vehicle":"Touring bike, 2–3 weeks","kind":"bike","color":"#ea580c","summary":"Down the Mekong from Laos's sleepy capital through riverside villages and temples, the Khmer ruins of Wat Phou, the coffee plateau near Pakse, the 4000 Islands with their waterfalls, across into Cambodia to see Irrawaddy dolphins at Kratie, and on to Phnom Penh. Flat, hot and friendly.","sources":[{"label":"Cycloscope: cycling Cambodia, Phnom Penh to the Lao border","url":"https://cycloscope.net/cycling-cambodia-phnom-penh-lao-border-kampong-cham-kratie-stung-treng/"},{"label":"Exo Travel: cycling southern Laos islands","url":"https://www.exotravel.com/tours/laos/cycling-southern-laos-islands-to-siem-reap/"}],"approximate":"Main towns; the roads are the router's choice.","km":1616,"bbox":[102.6133,11.573,106.1116,18.3994],"stops":[{"name":"Vientiane","place":"Vientiane, Laos","at":[17.9641,102.6134],"text":"Golden stupas and baguettes by the river."},{"name":"Paksan","place":"Paksan, Laos","at":[18.3924,103.6593],"text":"Rice fields along Route 13.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/NR13S%2C_Laos.jpg/500px-NR13S%2C_Laos.jpg","page":"Pakxan","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NR13S%2C_Laos.jpg","credit":"Phó Nháy","license":"Public domain"}},{"name":"Thakhek","place":"Thakhek, Laos","at":[17.3946,104.8065],"text":"Limestone karst on the horizon."},{"name":"Savannakhet","place":"Savannakhet, Laos","at":[16.5002,105.7156],"text":"A faded French colonial town.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Savannakhet1.JPG/500px-Savannakhet1.JPG","page":"Kaysone Phomvihane (city)","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Savannakhet1.JPG","credit":"No machine-readable author provided. Aaker assumed (based on copyright claims).